## What to deliver

Build and rig the aircraft up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a wide, flat fuselage carrying two spinning rotors
out on its sides, with an underslung cannon beneath the nose. **Author the three
required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands:
`rotor_spin` (a self-playing blur that whirls both rotors continuously), `hover` (a
buoyant up/down bob of the whole craft, eased so it floats rather than sawtooths), and
`strafe` (the cannon sweeping down to rake the ground and tipping back up, settling onto
the target with weight). The animations are the fixed contract — produce all three, by
those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When you are satisfied,
stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
